BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The New Year That Never Came
DTSTART:20250519T223000Z
DTEND:20250520T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20250519T223000Z
UID:Vd2oPD8N4H
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 138 mins (2h18m)\n\nSix lives intertwine in the days
  leading up to the 1989 Romanian revolution in this darkly funny ensemble 
 film about living under Communist rule. Winner of the 2024 Venice Film Fes
 tival’s Horizons Award and the Palm Springs New Voices/New Visions Grand
  Jury Prize.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-new-year-that-never-came
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jean Cocteau
DTSTART:20250520T020000Z
DTEND:20250520T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T020000Z
UID:dcW3XBPaPX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nLisa Immordino Vreeland (SIFF 202
 1’s Truman & Tennessee: An Intimate Conversation) constructs an astonish
 ing portrait of polymath Jean Cocteau—filmmaker\, playwright\, poet—to
 ld in his own words using his journals\, letters\, and artistic works. Pro
 ducer/Editor John Northrup scheduled to attend. Come early to the May 20 s
 creening to find out about ACT Contemporary Theatre's upcoming production 
 of "Twelfth Night" and get the chance to win a pair of tickets to the play
 !  Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/jean-cocteau\n\nAlso pla
 ying at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Tue 20 May\, 3:00 PM)\n\nFilm 
 is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Khartoum
DTSTART:20250520T043000Z
DTEND:20250520T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T043000Z
UID:u5dCkQgv91
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nThe Sudanese Civil War has displa
 ced over 10 million of its citizens. Now\, five survivors contend with the
 ir own memories\, and hope for a peaceful future\, using green screen tech
 nology to reenact their lives leading up to the military coup that forced 
 their evacuation. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/khartoum\
 n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Wed 21 May\, 1:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To Kill a Mongolian Horse
DTSTART:20250520T200000Z
DTEND:20250520T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T200000Z
UID:QVN3h4eveu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nIn this lovely and patient docudr
 ama set on the Mongolian steppes\, a champion horseback rider and herdsman
  struggles to maintain his family's ranch and traditional way of life in t
 he modern era.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/to-kill-a-mongolian-horse\
 n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:She’s The He
DTSTART:20250520T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T223000Z
UID:v85kCovBCf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 81 mins (1h21m)\n\nFirst-time director Siobhan McCar
 thy put together a cast and crew of almost entirely trans\, nonbinary\, an
 d queer people to make this Bottoms-esque teen satire about two seniors wh
 o pretend to be trans during their last week of high school\, only for one
  of them to find it suits them just fine. Director Siobhan McCarthy\, prod
 ucer Vic Brandt\, and producer Halley Albert scheduled to attend. Keep the
  cinematic trans hijinks going with a chance to win tickets to the Queer &
  Trans Film Festival at the May 19 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www
 .siff.net/festival/shes-the-he\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Upto
 wn House 3 (Mon 19 May\, 9:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baby Doe
DTSTART:20250521T010000Z
DTEND:20250521T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T010000Z
UID:YW7B1g7efW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nNearly 30 years after Gail aband
 oned her newborn son in the woods and returned to her conservative Christi
 an life\, the police came and arrested her for infanticide. From Tribeca-w
 inning documentarian Jessica Earnshaw (Hulu’s “Jacinta”). Director J
 essica Earnshaw and co-producer John Rudolf scheduled to attend. Sponsored
  by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/baby-doe\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • 
 SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Wed 21 May\, 3:45 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
